      "message": "I\u0027m not clear on how this signal will be controlled by the EC. I think this might be a new signal that is not used in legacy EC code. If it\u0027s not used in legacy EC code, then we wouldn\u0027t need an enun-name here as these names are only required for legacy code that refers to GPIO signals via their enum name.\n\nThe dedicated recovery power button GPIO gpio_gsc_ec_rec_btn_odl, does have an enum name in this file because the leagcy EC common code that handles recovery button presses assumes a gpio named  GPIO_RECOVERY_L will exist.",
