      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both the TCPC and PPC interrupt gpios are specified directly in the device tree. Here is what we have for port C1:\n\n\t\t/* a duplicate of the \u003c\u0026gpio_usb_c1_tcpc_int_odl\u003e node in\n\t\t * \"named-gpios\". This is the Zephyr preferred style,\n\t\t * the \"named-gpios\" node will be dealt with at a later date.\n\t\t */\n\t\tirq-gpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpioe 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW\u003e;\n\t\t\n\t\t/* a duplicate of the \u003c\u0026gpio_usb_c0_ppc_int_odl\u003e node in\n\t\t * \"named-gpios\". This is the Zephyr preferred style,\n\t\t * the \"named-gpios\" node will be dealt with at a later date.\n\t\t */\n\t\tirq-gpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio6 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW\u003e;\n\nBecause the TCPC/PPC interrupt handlers have already been converted to zephyr style, we won\u0027t need gpio enums for these signals. To clarify, these enums are added in Ovis for ports C0-C2, but that\u0027s because the zephyr style common interrupt handler code was introduced after the Ovis project was started.",
